1 NOTE {geni:about_me} As a converso in Portugal, Rachel used the name "Clara Roiz."
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT After Clara's father was burned alive at the stake in the central square of the Portuguese city of Coimbra. His wife managed to escape to France in 1618 with her daughter Clara and publicly resumed her observance of Jewish law. He
2 CONC r daughter, Clara, changed her name to Rachel and moved to the Netherlands in 1619, where she met Moshe (Moseh) Levy 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 1.2.1.1 Clara (Rachel/Raquel Rodrigues / Roiz o Maduro; b. 1596, Transcoso, Portugal; d. Amsterdam; she was born Clara but took the name Rachel (Raquel) when rebaptized into the Jewish faith.
2 CONT
2 CONT        = Moseh Levy o Maduro; d. 1 Jan 1640; aged 23 in 1619; he adopted the name Maduro to his existing surname of Levy; supposedly a descendant of Samuel Levi (Samuel Ha-Levi Abulafia; 1320-60), the Treasurer of King Pedro the C
2 CONC ruel of Aragon.
2 CONT
2 CONT /////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
2 CONT
2 CONT After Clara's father was burned alive at the stake in the central square of the Portuguese city of Coimbra. His wife managed to escape to France in 1618 and publicly resumed her observance of Jewish law. Her daughter, Clara, chang
2 CONC ed her name to Rachel and moved to the Netherlands in 1619, where she met Moshe (Moseh) Levy
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Fled with her mother to St. Jean de Luz in 1616, the same year that Anotnio Roiz o Maduro was burn at the stake, and took up the jewish religion of ther ancestors again. More About Mosseh Levy and Clara Rodriguez Madura: Marriage:
2 CONC  Circa 1619, Amsterdam, Netherlands Marriage recorded: 27 July 1622, Amsterdam, Netherlands Wittness: Samuel de Crasto and Isaacq Frances
2 CONT
