1 NOTE {geni:about_me} As a gesture of respect for the Maduro family, Moseh Levy (Levi) added Maduro to the name of his own family, which from that time on became known as Levy Maduro, nowadays just known as Maduro.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married to Rachel they became Jews, once again
2 CONT
2 CONT Moseh Levy was a descendant of Samuel (Shmuel) Ben Meir Ha-Levi Abulafia (c.1320-1360). Scion of an old Jewish family, Samuel Ha-Levi Abulafia was advisor and treasurer (tesorero real) to King Pedro I of Castile (1350-1369) (also 
2 CONC known as Pedro the Cruel) from 1350, and founder of a number of synagogues in the Kingdom of Castile Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Levi's fate took a turn for the worse in 1360, when King Pedro arrested and imprisoned him in Seville, having accused Samuel of taking part in a conspiracy against him. While in prison Samuel was tortured to death and all h
2 CONC is possessions were confiscated by the king including his house and the synagogue de Transito. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The street in Toledo where Samuel lived is called after him "Calle de Samuel Levi"
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
