1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Pedro Gomes de Abreu (c. 1390-1453) was a Portuguese nobleman, Lord of Regalados.[1] and Alcaide mor de Lapela.[2]
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Portugal, was the son of Lopo Gomes de Abreu and Inês de Soutomaior e Lima, daughter of Leonel de Lima (Viscount of Vila Nova de Cerveira), and Filipa da Cunha.[3] His Mistress was Catarina de Eça, daughter of Infante Fern
2 CONC ando, Lord of Eça and granddaughter of Peter I of Portugal.[4]
2 CONT References
2 CONT
2 CONT Indice Geral Dos Appellidos, Nomes Proprios, e cousas. 1749.
2 CONT fasc. 1. Abreus-Acciaiuolis. Cönego Fernando de Meneses Vaz, Ernesto Gonçalves, Luiz Peter.lon Clode. 1964.
2 CONT Revista portuguesa de história, Volume 31. 1996.
2 CONT Famílias do Rio Grande de São Pedro: Casa de Ornellas ou Dornelles, Volume 1. Saul Palma Souto, Homero Corrêa Pires Dornelles. 2004. ISBN 9788574304786.
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pedro_Gomes_de_Abreu
